  "description": "XEJJUS crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group I 2 2 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C120 H109 Cl10 Gd4 O28 P5. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.509-3.747 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.11-114.46°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C120 H109 Cl10 Gd4 O28 P5.",
